_GROUP_TOP_HELP=r"""
MagSurveyPy Archaeological Magnetometry Prospection Suite — Version 1.0.3
=======================================================================
Developed by Alexandru Hegyi, PhD
Website: https://alexandruhegyi.com
Email: alexandruhegyi@gmail.com
GitHub: https://github.com/alexandruhegyi

INSTALLATION
------------
Recommended installation after publication:
  python -m pip install magsurveypy

Install from an extracted source checkout:
  python -m pip install .

Both forms create the `mspy` command automatically.
To uninstall:
  python -m pip uninstall magsurveypy

Conda is an alternative environment route; see INSTALL.md or `mspy guide installation`.

WORKFLOW
--------
MagSurveyPy uses project-based, acquisition-class terminology. New project folders
are Multichannel, TotalField and Fluxgate rather than manufacturer-specific names.
Original field data are never overwritten. Derived processing, analysis, figures,
GIS export and Web GIS are separate and reproducible stages.

PUBLIC COMMAND GROUPS
---------------------
  project   Create/import/configure projects and inspect project state.
  survey    Initial processing for multichannel and gridded magnetic surveys.
  layout    Explicit local-grid geometry editor and validator.
  process   Core derived stages: interpolate, clean, enhance, segment, thin.
  filter    Explicit observation-level or raster-level filters with audit outputs.
  analyze   Survey/line/sensor/raster/spectrum/stage diagnostics and graphs.
  figure    Reproducible scientific and publication figures.
  export    GIS/cartographic deliverables: map, reproject, contours, bundle.
  web       Interactive local Web GIS for interpretation and profile analysis.
  gnss      GNSS/RINEX/PPK utilities.
  tools     Dependency diagnostics and complete help generation.
  guide     Scientific guides and workflow explanations.
  help      Detailed help for one group or command.

PROJECT CREATION
----------------
  mspy project init --project Site --category multichannel
  mspy project init --project Site --category total-field
  mspy project init --project Site --category fluxgate
  mspy project init --project Site --category mixed

Import matching field data with:
  mspy project import --project Site --input /path/to/data --type multichannel
  mspy project import --project Site --input /path/to/data --type total-field
  mspy project import --project Site --input /path/to/data --type fluxgate

CORE SURVEY COMMANDS
--------------------
  mspy survey multichannel --project Site --format auto --workflow standard
  mspy survey grid --project Site --protocol total-field --workflow archaeology
  mspy survey grid --project Site --protocol fluxgate --workflow archaeology

Optional gradients from split-sensor total-field files:
  mspy survey grid --project Site --protocol total-field --gradient vertical --sensor-separation 0.50
  mspy survey grid --project Site --protocol total-field --gradient horizontal --sensor-separation 0.50

If an exported total-field file contains only one final READING column, omit
`--gradient`; the ordinary total-field workflow is unchanged. Gradient derivation
never guesses sensor separation.

CORE WORKFLOW
-------------
  1. project init / import / config
  2. survey multichannel OR survey grid --protocol total-field|fluxgate
  3. analyze survey
  4. process interpolate / clean / enhance as scientifically justified
  5. filter only when an explicit correction is required
  6. analyze again and inspect removed/difference products
  7. figure for papers/reports
  8. export or use web for interactive GIS

LICENSE AND WARRANTY
--------------------
MagSurveyPy is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License and is provided "AS IS",
without warranty. Users are responsible for validating survey metadata, processing
choices, coordinate systems, outputs, and scientific interpretation.

HELP
----
  mspy <group> --help
  mspy help <group> <command>
  mspy guide installation
  mspy guide projects
  mspy tools help-all
"""

